From b5082ad0b0b2b3ef6059b4b3654c4ed9c554985d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Khadas Edge1 Android TV <edge1@localhost>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 16:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dumb_driver: NV12 scanout on rockchip

Khadas Edge1 (RK3399), Android 14. AOSP builds the generic gralloc
(libminigbm_gralloc) without DRV_ROCKCHIP, so rockchip-drm gets the dumb
driver, whose NV12 is texture, video and camera only. SurfaceFlinger asks
for HW_COMPOSER on every video layer, and a flexible YUV buffer resolves to
NV12 - so the allocation fails outright. Card 27, from the FFmpeg Codec2
decoder's first NV12 frame (external/ffmpeg_codec2 patch 0003):

  Failed to allocate. Unsupported combination: pixel format:YCBCR_420_888,
  drm format:DRM_FOURCC_9999, usage:... GPU_TEXTURE | HW_COMPOSER
  GraphicBufferAllocator: Failed to allocate (3840 x 2160) ... usage 933

and the decoder fell back to YV12, which the resolve helper takes scanout
off: no video frame could ever reach a display plane.

Rockchip's VOPs do scan out NV12 (formats_win_full: the RK3399 big VOP's
win0 and win1, with scaling), as minigbm's own rockchip backend says. The
combination gets BO_USE_SCANOUT for "rockchip" only; every other dumb
driver is unchanged. Checked on the host with the core files and a small
harness: FLEX_YCbCr_420_888 with SW_READ/WRITE_OFTEN | TEXTURE | SCANOUT is
"Unsupported combination" before and supported after for rockchip, still
unsupported for vkms; YV12 unchanged.
---
 dumb_driver.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dumb_driver.c b/dumb_driver.c
index f74d237..230e8d5 100644
--- a/dumb_driver.c
+++ b/dumb_driver.c
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <errno.h>
+#include <string.h>
 
 #include "drv_helpers.h"
 #include "drv_priv.h"
@@ -49,6 +50,15 @@ static int dumb_driver_init(struct driver *drv)
 				   BO_USE_CAMERA_READ | BO_USE_CAMERA_WRITE);
 	drv_modify_combination(drv, DRM_FORMAT_NV21, &LINEAR_METADATA, BO_USE_HW_VIDEO_ENCODER);
 
+	/*
+	 * Rockchip's VOPs scan out NV12 (formats_win_full: RK3399 big VOP win0/win1),
+	 * and without DRV_ROCKCHIP this driver is all "rockchip" gets. Video layers ask
+	 * for HW_COMPOSER, so a flexible YUV (NV12) buffer without scanout cannot be
+	 * allocated for one at all.
+	 */
+	if (!strcmp(drv->backend->name, "rockchip"))
+		drv_modify_combination(drv, DRM_FORMAT_NV12, &LINEAR_METADATA, BO_USE_SCANOUT);
+
 	return drv_modify_linear_combinations(drv);
 }
 
